        "body": "Close offshore continuity test only when the destination value in the continuity plan, the approver, and the time of the final check are all visible. If the destination is another team, require an acknowledgment. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Record the close reason with the same codes used in the exception queue. In the offshore continuity test queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception.\n\nDo not mark complete until the check is repeatable by another reviewer. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. For offshore continuity test, the working file keeps the test plan and the participant roster beside the decision note.\n\nDo not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Every offshore continuity test handoff names the continuity lead and the field in the continuity plan that will confirm the change."
